  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Injection Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Injection Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Injection Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Injection== = untrusted input crossing a trust boundary, run as code by an interpreter",
                "{blue:SQL engine}, {green:shell}, {purple:filesystem}, {orange:HTTP client}",
                "Root cause: ==data channel== and ==code channel== mixed in one string",
                "Fix: **keep them separate**, not clean the string"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Source to Sink",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Source",
                    "sub": "query, header, cookie, JSON, filename",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Boundary",
                    "sub": "untrusted text in a string",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sink",
                    "sub": "query exec, shell, file open, fetch",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The quote ends the string; `OR '1'='1` is always true",
                "Result: ==every row== comes back"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "name = \"' OR '1'='1\"",
                "print(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name='\" + name + \"'\")"
              ],
              "note": "input became SQL structure"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name='' OR '1'='1'"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never let data become code. ==Separate== beats sanitize."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Escaping vs parameters?** Escaping patches one string; parameters never mix data into code",
                "**Sink?** The call that executes input: query exec, shell, file open, fetch",
                "**Client-side validation?** Attackers skip the browser and call the API directly"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "SQL Injection and Parameterized Queries",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "SQL Injection and Parameterized Queries",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Parameterized Queries",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Template== and ==values== are sent separately",
                "Values stay **data**, never query structure",
                "Python `%s`; JDBC `PreparedStatement` with `?`",
                "{red:Unsafe}: f-string, `+`, `String.format` in SQL"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=%s\", (uid,))",
                "cur.execute(f\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id={uid}\")"
              ],
              "note": "first is safe, second is injectable"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Attack Types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Data leaves",
                "Examples"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**In-band**",
                  "in the response",
                  "UNION, error-based"
                ],
                [
                  "**Blind**",
                  "inferred from true/false or delay",
                  "boolean, time-based"
                ],
                [
                  "**Out-of-band**",
                  "sent via DNS or HTTP",
                  "exfiltration"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Identifiers",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Placeholders bind ==values only==",
                "Not table names, column names or ORDER BY direction",
                "Allowlist those identifiers in code instead"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "SORT = {\"name\": \"name\", \"new\": \"created_at\"}",
                "col = SORT.get(by, \"name\")",
                "cur.execute(f\"SELECT * FROM users ORDER BY {col}\")"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**How do prepared statements stop injection?** Values are never parsed as SQL.",
                "**Parameterize a table name?** No; allowlist it.",
                "**Blind SQLi?** Infers data from true/false or delays.",
                "**Why least privilege?** Limits damage: no DROP, no other schemas."
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ORM Pitfalls and Command Injection",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ORM Pitfalls and Command Injection",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. ORM Escape Hatches",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "ORMs ==parameterize by default==",
                "Raw escape hatches reopen injection",
                "Risk = the ==string you build==, not the library"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "ORM",
                "Unsafe call"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Django",
                  "`.raw()`, `.extra()`"
                ],
                [
                  "SQLAlchemy",
                  "`text(f\"...\")`"
                ],
                [
                  "Sequelize",
                  "`query` with interpolation"
                ],
                [
                  "Rails",
                  "`where(\"name='#{x}'\")`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "q = text(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=:id\")",
                "conn.execute(q, {\"id\": uid})"
              ],
              "note": "safe: bind params"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Operator Injection",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Body passed straight into a filter",
                "NoSQL: attacker sends `{\"$ne\": null}`, matches anything",
                "Mass assignment: body sets `is_admin=true`",
                "Fix: allowed fields only"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Command Injection",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Input in a shell: `;` `|` `&&` `$()` backticks add commands",
                "`ping 8.8.8.8; rm -rf /` runs both",
                "Bug: `shell=True` or `os.system` with input",
                "Fix: argument array, `shell=False`, allowlist and validate args"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import subprocess",
                "host = \"8.8.8.8\"",
                "r = subprocess.run([\"ping\", \"-c\", \"1\", host],",
                "                   shell=False, capture_output=True)"
              ],
              "note": "host stays one argument"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**ORM immune?** No: raw calls and built strings still inject",
                "**List vs string?** No shell parses a list, so input stays one argument",
                "**Operator injection?** Input like `{\"$ne\": null}` becomes a query operator"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Path Traversal, SSRF and Input Validation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Path Traversal, SSRF and Input Validation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Path traversal",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`../`, ==%2e%2e%2f==, absolute paths, symlinks escape the base dir",
                "e.g. `/download?file=../../etc/passwd`",
                "Blocking `../` alone is **bypassable**",
                "Fix: ==realpath==, then check it starts with BASE; or map IDs to filenames"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import os",
                "from urllib.parse import unquote",
                "BASE = os.path.realpath(\"/srv/files\")",
                "name = unquote(\"%2e%2e/%2e%2e/etc/passwd\")",
                "p = os.path.realpath(os.path.join(BASE, name))",
                "print(p.startswith(BASE + os.sep))"
              ],
              "note": "decode first, resolve, then compare with the resolved BASE"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "False"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. SSRF",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Server fetches a user-supplied URL, so attackers reach internal services",
                "Cloud metadata `http://169.254.169.254/` leaks instance credentials",
                "==Allowlist== hosts",
                "Resolve DNS, block private, loopback, link-local IPs",
                "Re-validate every redirect (stops 302-to-internal)",
                "Pin the validated IP (stops DNS rebinding)",
                "Disable `file://`, `gopher://` schemes",
                "Use ==IMDSv2== on AWS"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Input validation",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Allowlist== (type, length, format, range) beats blocklist",
                "Validate **server-side**",
                "Canonicalize (decode) before checking"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Defense in depth",
              "text": "Validation never replaces parameterization or output encoding."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes and Fixes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Mistakes and Fixes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Four mistakes, four fixes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Escaping or quote-stripping, not parameters",
                  "==Bind parameters== everywhere"
                ],
                [
                  "Concatenated ORDER BY, table or column names",
                  "Map input to a fixed ==allowlist=="
                ],
                [
                  "Client-side only, or checked before decoding",
                  "==Server-side== check after canonicalization"
                ],
                [
                  "DB account can DROP or read all schemas",
                  "==Least privilege==, read-only users, generic errors, no SQL or stack traces"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "SORTS = {\"name\": \"name\", \"new\": \"created_at\"}",
                "col = SORTS.get(sort, \"created_at\")",
                "cur.execute(f\"SELECT * FROM t WHERE id=%s ORDER BY {col}\", (uid,))"
              ],
              "note": "values bound, identifier picked from the allowlist"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Defenses and review",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Parameterize",
                    "sub": "strongest",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Allowlist",
                    "sub": "validate",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Least privilege",
                    "sub": "limit damage",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Safe errors",
                    "sub": "no leaks",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Review**: hunt string-built SQL, `shell=True`, `os.system`, raw ORM calls fed by input",
                "**SAST** flags source-to-sink flows; **DAST** and **fuzzing** send payloads at live endpoints",
                "**Logs**: alert on SQL errors, 500 spikes, blocked `../` paths"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Escaping cleans the string; ==parameters== keep data out of the code channel."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
